    "name": "owner-ce",
    "captureSha256": "c1aafd70f290003ecc23d70c1410254b8de52283bc3146440a5c50e1c188aa87",
    "markdown": "No Kubernetes, operator CRD, or license key is needed. The CE quickstart runs entirely with Docker Compose ([Do I need an account?](/docs/ce/faq#do-i-need-an-account)):\n\n```bash\ngit clone --branch v0.6 https://github.com/hev/layer.git\ncd layer\nexport TURBOPUFFER_API_KEY=\"\"\nexport GATEWAY_IMAGE=hevlayer/layer-gateway:edge\ndocker compose up -d --wait\ncurl --fail http://localhost:8080/health\n```\n\nThe Compose bundle includes Postgres with `pgvector` and `pg_search` \u2014 no external database, no signup, and no bearer token required for the local connection ([Local development and CI](/docs/ce/install#local-development-and-ci)). Setting `TURBOPUFFER_API_KEY=\"\"` selects local Postgres; a non-blank key routes to Turbopuffer instead ([1. Clone and start](/docs/ce/quickstart#1-clone-and-start)). The source is licensed under BSL 1.1 \u2014 the local quickstart needs no runtime license key ([Licensing](/docs/ce/licensing)).",
