  {
    "name": "owner-pro",
    "captureSha256": "1c9243d915a3a9ff87ee7555255836335577682e0e5a19ce695db320a8abf6dd",
    "markdown": "The operator (`layer-operator`) is deployed as part of the Helm chart at `infra/helm/layer/`, which installs `layer-gateway`, `layer-operator`, and `layer-document-cache` together, along with the CRD types themselves \u2014 no separate CRD apply step is needed. On a bring-your-own cluster (the chart is not in a public Helm repo), run:\n\n```sh\nhelm upgrade --install layer ./infra/helm/layer \\\n  --namespace layer --create-namespace \\\n  -f ./infra/helm/layer/values-demo.yaml \\\n  -f values.customer.yaml\n```\n\nSee [Helm](/docs/pro/install#helm) and [what gets installed](/docs/pro/install#what-gets-installed) for the full chart surface.\n\nThe [operator](/docs/pro/kubernetes/operator) reconciles [five CRD kinds](/docs/pro/kubernetes/operator#crds):\n- **VectorStore** \u2014 upstream endpoint, credential Secret, inbound auth policy\n- **Index** \u2014 one per managed namespace (snapshot policy, embedding profile, scan threads, cache posture)\n- **InfraRules** \u2014 compute pools and shared scaling policy\n- **Pipeline** \u2014 staged row-ingestion work\n- **Function** \u2014 stateless UDFs over existing index rows\n\nThe [gateway and operator are fully decoupled](/docs/pro/kubernetes/operator#relationship-to-the-gateway): the gateway reads CRD status to inform serving but never writes to CRDs, so the gateway keeps serving if the operator restarts or lags.\n\nFor [scheduling](/docs/pro/kubernetes/operator#scheduling-and-node-pools), built-in pools (`cpu`, `cpu-large`, `gpu`) are active when no `InfraRules/default` object exists, selecting chart-rendered Karpenter worker nodes via `layer.hev.dev/node-role=worker-cpu` / `worker-gpu`. Apply `InfraRules/default` to customize resources, node selectors, tolerations, or replica ceilings cluster-wide rather than per workload.",
