    "name": "reviewer-ce",
    "captureSha256": "534d870d7a86861144c08c69737946cbb9fc5afa17197a54dd2aca03b36b3ed4",
    "markdown": "No Kubernetes operator is required \u2014 Docker Compose with Docker is everything you need.\n\nClone the `v0.6` branch, set an empty `TURBOPUFFER_API_KEY` (this selects the bundled Postgres instead of Turbopuffer), and start Compose:\n\n```bash\ngit clone --branch v0.6 https://github.com/hev/layer.git\ncd layer\nexport TURBOPUFFER_API_KEY=\"\"\nexport GATEWAY_IMAGE=hevlayer/layer-gateway:edge\ndocker compose up -d --wait\n```\n\nThe bundle includes Postgres with `pgvector` and `pg_search` \u2014 no external database setup needed. `--wait` blocks until the Compose health check passes. Once it returns, verify the gateway directly with:\n\n```bash\ncurl --fail http://localhost:8080/health\n```\n\nThe [health endpoint](/docs/ce/observability#health) requires no authentication and is also the right check to use in CI. No account, API key, or license key is required \u2014 the [local quickstart](/docs/ce/quickstart#1-clone-and-start) runs entirely without signup. Row data persists in a Docker volume across restarts; `docker compose down` stops services but keeps the volume. The [CE Compose bundle](/docs/ce/install#local-development-and-ci) is the supported path for local development and CI alike.",
