  {
    "name": "reviewer-pro",
    "captureSha256": "dc799dfe00cc687d1ef192545ce15e5ef1852adae1c90cb5c7d4ea184e9223d3",
    "markdown": "The [operator](/docs/pro/kubernetes/operator) is the Kubernetes control-plane component that reconciles all declarative Layer state. It watches five CRD kinds \u2014 VectorStore, Index, InfraRules, Pipeline, and Function \u2014 and creates or updates the corresponding cluster objects (Deployments, KEDA ScaledObjects, Secrets) to match desired spec. The operator and gateway are deliberately decoupled: neither sits in the other's hot path, so the gateway keeps serving if the operator restarts or lags. The relationship is one-directional and read-only \u2014 the gateway reads CRD status to inform what it serves but never writes back to CRDs.\n\nA [VectorStore](/docs/pro/kubernetes/vectorstore-crd) is the gateway's upstream connection record. It declares the store kind, endpoint URL and region, the credential `Secret` reference holding the upstream API key, and the inbound auth policy the gateway enforces on client requests. Multiple VectorStores can coexist in one install, and the gateway builds one upstream client per declared store.\n\nAn [Index](/docs/pro/kubernetes/index-crd) represents one logical namespace exposed through the gateway. It declares which VectorStore backs it (via `spec.backend.storeRef`, defaulting to the store marked `default`), the upstream namespace name (defaulting to the Index's own name), the distance metric, snapshot policy, cache posture, embedding identity, and scan fan-out.\n\nThe three are related as a hierarchy: the operator reconciles all of them; a VectorStore is the *connection* (credentials and endpoint); an Index is the *namespace configuration* that points at a VectorStore. When a request arrives, the gateway resolves the namespace \u2192 finds its Index \u2192 reads the `storeRef` \u2192 routes to that VectorStore's upstream client. Namespaces with no matching Index fall back to the default VectorStore. Two Index objects cannot resolve to the same upstream namespace, and the operator marks an Index `Ready=False` with a `MetricMismatch` reason if the declared distance metric isn't supported by the target store.",
